exports[`orchestrate — contracts & runbook > golden shape (paths normalized) > RUNBOOK.md 1`] = `
"# ultra11y — sequential RUNBOOK (eco / no-subagent fallback)

Run: \`<RUN>\` · Engine: \`node <ENGINE>\`

Generated by \`ultra11y orchestrate\` from the CURRENT run state. This sequential path is
correctness-identical to the multi-agent workflows — same worklists, same contracts, same
fail-closed gates; only wall-clock differs. Fan-out is an optimization, not a requirement.

## Phase status

| Phase | Worklist | Status | Produce it with |
|---|---|---|---|
| adjudicate | \`<RUN>/ADJUDICATE.todo.json\` | ready (4 item(s)) | \`node <ENGINE> verify --manual --in <RUN>/audit-latest.json --out <RUN>\` |
| verify-report | \`<RUN>/VERIFY.todo.json\` | ready (2 item(s)) | \`node <ENGINE> verify --report <report.md> --in <RUN>/audit-latest.json --standard wcag --out <RUN>\` |

## The loop (play every role yourself, one item at a time)

1. **Audit** (if not done): \`node <ENGINE> audit "<globs>" --graph --out <RUN>\` → \`<RUN>/audit-latest.json\`.
2. **Adjudicate the residual criteria** — \`node <ENGINE> verify --manual --in <RUN>/audit-latest.json --out <RUN>\` writes \`<RUN>/ADJUDICATE.todo.json\`. For EVERY item, apply \`<RUN>/orchestration/agents/adjudicator.md\` yourself (read the evidence, rule C/NC/NA/manual, fill the required justification/findings/reason IN the todo file). Then fold — gated per verdict, so a refusal costs its own criterion and no other: \`node <ENGINE> verify --apply <RUN>/ADJUDICATE.todo.json --in <RUN>/audit-latest.json --out <RUN>\`. Add \`--ledger .ultra11y/verdicts/<standard>.json\` to RECORD the verdicts that landed, so CI can replay them without a model; \`--strict\` restores the old all-or-nothing fold.
3. **Report**: \`node <ENGINE> report --in <RUN>/audit-latest.json --out <RUN>\`.
4. **Verify the report's claims** — \`node <ENGINE> verify --report <report.md> --in <RUN>/audit-latest.json --standard wcag --out <RUN>\` writes \`<RUN>/VERIFY.todo.json\` (and \`<RUN>/VERIFY.context.json\`, the context it was built from): the report's non-conformities AND the conformities the adjudication cleared in that audit. For EVERY entry, apply \`<RUN>/orchestration/agents/refuter.md\` yourself (open file:line, verdict supported/partial/refuted/unsupported + note IN the todo file). Then: \`node <ENGINE> verify --apply <RUN>/VERIFY.todo.json --report <report.md> --in <RUN>/audit-latest.json --standard wcag\`. Generation and apply carry the SAME \`--in\`, \`--standard\` and conformity source (\`--conformities <file>\` / \`--no-conformities\`, if you used one): a list built from another source covers other claims, and \`--max-verify 0\` does not fix that — regenerate it. \`--no-conformities\` or an explicit \`--max-verify\` makes a PARTIAL trial; do not present it as covering the audit.
5. **Gate**: \`node <ENGINE> check --report <report.md> --standard wcag --semantic --verdicts <RUN>/VERIFY.todo.json\` must exit 0 before presenting anything.
6. **Fix & re-audit**: \`node <ENGINE> fix "<globs>" --write --iterate\`, hand-apply the judgment fixes, then loop from step 1 until the gate stays green.

## With subagents — the same phases, fanned out

\`orchestrate --run <RUN> --phase <p>\` writes \`<RUN>/orchestration/<p>.batches.json\` (every batch as data: its items, the schema its answer must match, its output path and the fold) and one self-contained prompt per batch under \`<RUN>/orchestration/<p>/<batch-id>.md\`. On any harness: hand each prompt file VERBATIM to one subagent, save each returned JSON at that batch's \`output\` (\`<RUN>/orchestration/out/<p>/<batch-id>.json\`), fill the worklist from those answers yourself, then run the phase's fold above. On Claude Code, \`Workflow({ scriptPath: "<RUN>/orchestration/<p>.workflow.mjs" })\` dispatches the same batches in one call. You stay the sole writer either way.

The batches of the current worklists, as \`orchestrate\` without \`--eco\` writes them:

- **adjudicate** — 1 batch(es): \`<RUN>/orchestration/adjudicate.batches.json\`
- **verify-report** — 1 batch(es): \`<RUN>/orchestration/verify-report.batches.json\`
"
`;

exports[`orchestrate — contracts & runbook > golden shape (paths normalized) > adjudicate.workflow.mjs 1`] = `
"export const meta = {"name":"ultra11y-adjudicate","description":"Adjudicate the 4 residual judgment criterion(ia) of an ultra11y audit (fan-out, fail-closed fold)","phases":[{"title":"Adjudicate"}]}

// NOT a plain Node script: launch via the Workflow tool — Workflow({ scriptPath: "<RUN>/orchestration/adjudicate.workflow.mjs" }).
// Emitted by \`ultra11y orchestrate\` from the CURRENT worklist. The worklist is the source
// of truth: if it changes, re-run \`orchestrate --phase adjudicate\` before launching.
// One adapter of <RUN>/orchestration/adjudicate.batches.json — the harness-neutral batches.

// Constants for THIS run (injected at emit time; no Date.now/Math.random in this harness).
const RUN = "<RUN>"
const ENGINE = "<ENGINE>"
const WORKLIST = "<RUN>/ADJUDICATE.todo.json"
const AGENTS = RUN + '/orchestration/agents'
const BATCHES = [["1.1.1","1.2.2","1.3.3","1.4.4"]]
const SCHEMA = {"type":"object","required":["verdicts"],"properties":{"verdicts":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","required":["criteriaId","verdict"],"properties":{"criteriaId":{"type":"string"},"verdict":{"enum":["C","NC","NA","manual"]},"justification":{"type":"string","description":"REQUIRED for C and NA"},"citations":{"type":"array","description":"REQUIRED for C, and for NA when evidence was presented: the evidence items you cleared, \`file\`/\`line\` copied verbatim from this criterion's own evidence[]","items":{"type":"object","required":["file","line"],"properties":{"file":{"type":"string"},"line":{"type":"number"},"selector":{"type":"string"},"snippet":{"type":"string"}}}},"reason":{"type":["string","null"],"enum":["needs-rendered-dom","undecidable",null],"description":"REQUIRED for a still-manual verdict"},"findings":{"type":"array","description":"REQUIRED (>=1, groundable) for NC","items":{"type":"object","required":["file","line","message","normativeRef"],"properties":{"file":{"type":"string"},"line":{"type":"integer"},"selector":{"type":"string"},"message":{"type":"string"},"snippet":{"type":"string"},"severity":{"enum":["bloquant","majeur","mineur"]},"normativeRef":{"type":"string","description":"The precise failed test of the ACTIVE standard. WCAG core: a success-criterion id (e.g. '1.1.1'). Country standard: a test OF THIS ITEM'S OWN CRITERION (e.g. '11.2.1' on item 11.2) — a WCAG id looks alike but denotes an unrelated test and is rejected."}}}},"pages":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":{"type":"object","required":["verdict"],"properties":{"verdict":{"enum":["C","NC","NA"],"description":"REQUIRED — a page verdict is C, NC or NA; there is no per-page manual"},"justification":{"type":"string","description":"REQUIRED for a per-page C and NA"},"citations":{"type":"array","description":"REQUIRED for a per-page C, and for a per-page NA when evidence was presented","items":{"type":"object","required":["file","line"],"properties":{"file":{"type":"string"},"line":{"type":"number"},"selector":{"type":"string"},"snippet":{"type":"string"}}}},"findings":{"type":"array","description":"REQUIRED (>=1, groundable) for a per-page NC","items":{"type":"object","required":["file","line","message","normativeRef"],"properties":{"file":{"type":"string"},"line":{"type":"integer"},"selector":{"type":"string"},"message":{"type":"string"},"snippet":{"type":"string"},"severity":{"enum":["bloquant","majeur","mineur"]},"normativeRef":{"type":"string","description":"The precise failed test of the ACTIVE standard. WCAG core: a success-criterion id (e.g. '1.1.1'). Country standard: a test OF THIS ITEM'S OWN CRITERION (e.g. '11.2.1' on item 11.2) — a WCAG id looks alike but denotes an unrelated test and is rejected."}}}}}},"description":"OPTIONAL on a decided C/NC/NA verdict: per-page outcomes keyed by AUDITED PAGE id (the worklist header lists them). Each page verdict passes the same gate as the run-level verdict, scoped to that page: every citation and finding names the page's own capture (.ultra11y/pages/<id>/dom.html) or a source it declares. A page NC needs a run-wide NC; no page C/NA where a run-wide NC finding sits. A page left unnamed keeps the run-wide verdict — there is no per-page manual. A page whose subject is clean gets its own C; a page whose subject fails gets its own NC."}}}}}}

function contract(name, extra) {
  return 'Read and follow the dispatch contract at ' + AGENTS + '/' + name + '.md VERBATIM.\\n'
    + 'Constants: RUN=' + RUN + '  ENGINE=' + ENGINE + '  WORKLIST=' + WORKLIST + '.\\n'
    + 'Invoke the engine only by its ABSOLUTE path: node ' + ENGINE + ' <cmd> — read-only commands only.'
    + (extra ? '\\n' + extra : '')
}

log('ultra11y adjudicate: ' + "4" + ' item(s) across ' + BATCHES.length + ' agent(s)')

phase("Adjudicate")
const results = await pipeline(BATCHES, (batch, _item, i) =>
  agent(contract('adjudicator', 'ITEMS=' + batch.join(',')), { label: 'adjudicate:' + (i + 1), phase: "Adjudicate", agentType: 'general-purpose', schema: SCHEMA }))

// One-writer rule: this workflow only COLLECTS verdict fragments. The main agent folds
// them into WORKLIST (fill each item's fields from the matching fragment), then runs:
//   node <ENGINE> verify --apply <RUN>/ADJUDICATE.todo.json --in <RUN>/audit-latest.json --out <RUN>
return { phase: "adjudicate", worklist: WORKLIST, results: results.filter(Boolean) }
"
`;

exports[`orchestrate — contracts & runbook > golden shape (paths normalized) > refuter.md 1`] = `
"# Contract: refuter

You are an adversarial skeptic verifying the non-conformities of an ultra11y report. Your job is to try to REFUTE each claim: assume it is wrong until the source proves it.

Worklist: \`<RUN>/VERIFY.todo.json\` (a JSON array; each entry has \`n\`, \`criteriaId\`, \`file\`, \`line\`, \`selector\`, \`claim\`). Handle ONLY the entries whose \`n\` is named in your prompt (\`ITEMS=<n,…>\`).

For EACH of your entries:

1. Open \`file\` at \`line\` and read the cited element (\`selector\`) in its real context.
2. Judge the claim against the source:
   - \`supported\` — the cited code violates the criterion exactly as claimed.
   - \`partial\` — a real issue, but the claim overstates it (wrong element, wrong scope, exaggerated count).
   - \`unsupported\` — the source does not establish the claim.
   - \`refuted\` — the source contradicts the claim.
   When unsure, choose the HARSHER verdict — a false pass is worse than a false fail.
3. \`note\` is REQUIRED — one line grounded in what you read (quote or paraphrase the decisive code).

Return (structured output): \`{ "verdicts": [{ "n", "verdict", "note" }] }\` — your ITEMS only.

## Return, don't write

Return ONLY the structured output specified above. Do NOT write, edit, or delete any file; do NOT run any engine command that writes (\`verify --apply\`, \`fix --write\`, \`audit --out\`, \`init\`). The orchestrator is the sole writer — it folds your verdicts into the worklist itself and runs the apply gate. Exceptions: if your harness gives you no way to return structured output, write that JSON ONLY to the output path your batch prompt names (\`<RUN>/orchestration/out/<phase>/<batch-id>.json\`); if a justification is prose too large to return, write ONLY to \`<RUN>/orchestration/out/<role>-<batch>.md\` (a file namespaced to you alone) and return its path.
"
`;

exports[`orchestrate — contracts & runbook > golden shape (paths normalized) > verify-report-01.md 1`] = `
"# ultra11y verify-report — batch verify-report-01 (refuter)

You are one subagent of an ultra11y fan-out: batch 1 of 1 of the « Verify » phase. This file is your whole brief — nothing else needs to be passed to you.

ITEMS=1,2

Constants: RUN=<RUN>  ENGINE=<ENGINE>  WORKLIST=<RUN>/VERIFY.todo.json.
Invoke the engine only by its ABSOLUTE path: \`node <ENGINE> <cmd>\` — read-only commands only.

## Your items

The 2 worklist entries you rule on, copied from \`<RUN>/VERIFY.todo.json\`. Handle these and no others.

\`\`\`json
[
  {
    "n": 1,
    "criteriaId": "1.1.1",
    "file": "src/page.html",
    "line": 2,
    "selector": "img",
    "claim": "claim 1",
    "verdict": null,
    "note": ""
  },
  {
    "n": 2,
    "criteriaId": "1.1.1",
    "file": "src/page.html",
    "line": 3,
    "selector": "img",
    "claim": "claim 2",
    "verdict": null,
    "note": ""
  }
]
\`\`\`

## What you return

Exactly ONE JSON object that validates against the schema below, covering your ITEMS only — as your structured output if your harness has one, otherwise as your final message with nothing before or after it.

The orchestrator saves that object at \`<RUN>/orchestration/out/verify-report/verify-report-01.json\` and folds it. If your harness gives you no way to return it, write it to that path yourself: the file is namespaced to this batch, and it is the ONLY file you may write.

\`\`\`json
{
  "type": "object",
  "required": [
    "verdicts"
  ],
  "properties": {
    "verdicts": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "type": "object",
        "required": [
          "n",
          "verdict",
          "note"
        ],
        "properties": {
          "n": {
            "type": "integer"
          },
          "verdict": {
            "enum": [
              "supported",
              "partial",
              "refuted",
              "unsupported"
            ]
          },
          "note": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "one line grounded in the source you read"
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
\`\`\`

## Your contract (\`<RUN>/orchestration/agents/refuter.md\`, inline)

# Contract: refuter

You are an adversarial skeptic verifying the non-conformities of an ultra11y report. Your job is to try to REFUTE each claim: assume it is wrong until the source proves it.

Worklist: \`<RUN>/VERIFY.todo.json\` (a JSON array; each entry has \`n\`, \`criteriaId\`, \`file\`, \`line\`, \`selector\`, \`claim\`). Handle ONLY the entries whose \`n\` is named in your prompt (\`ITEMS=<n,…>\`).

For EACH of your entries:

1. Open \`file\` at \`line\` and read the cited element (\`selector\`) in its real context.
2. Judge the claim against the source:
   - \`supported\` — the cited code violates the criterion exactly as claimed.
   - \`partial\` — a real issue, but the claim overstates it (wrong element, wrong scope, exaggerated count).
   - \`unsupported\` — the source does not establish the claim.
   - \`refuted\` — the source contradicts the claim.
   When unsure, choose the HARSHER verdict — a false pass is worse than a false fail.
3. \`note\` is REQUIRED — one line grounded in what you read (quote or paraphrase the decisive code).

Return (structured output): \`{ "verdicts": [{ "n", "verdict", "note" }] }\` — your ITEMS only.

## Return, don't write

Return ONLY the structured output specified above. Do NOT write, edit, or delete any file; do NOT run any engine command that writes (\`verify --apply\`, \`fix --write\`, \`audit --out\`, \`init\`). The orchestrator is the sole writer — it folds your verdicts into the worklist itself and runs the apply gate. Exceptions: if your harness gives you no way to return structured output, write that JSON ONLY to the output path your batch prompt names (\`<RUN>/orchestration/out/<phase>/<batch-id>.json\`); if a justification is prose too large to return, write ONLY to \`<RUN>/orchestration/out/<role>-<batch>.md\` (a file namespaced to you alone) and return its path.

## After you — the orchestrator's step, not yours

The main agent is the sole writer. Once every batch of this phase has answered, it fills each worklist item from the matching answer and runs the fail-closed fold:

\`node <ENGINE> verify --apply <RUN>/VERIFY.todo.json --report <report.md> --in <RUN>/audit-latest.json --standard wcag\`
"
`;
